        "body": "<!-- greptile_comment -->\n\n<details open><summary><h3>Greptile Summary</h3></summary>\n\nThis PR adds a new file `09_test_github_wbe/git copy.py` containing a Pydantic `Employee` model and a small decorator demonstration.\n\n- The file defines decorators `a` and `b` twice each; the second definitions silently overwrite the first, making the first pair dead code and obscuring any intended distinction between them.\n- The `Employee` model uses a mismatched `description` on the `age` field and a deprecated `example` kwarg on `salary`, along with unused `List` and `Literal` imports.\n</details>\n\n<details open><summary><h3>Confidence Score: 4/5</h3></summary>\n\nThe file is a standalone learning/demo script with no production wiring, but the duplicate decorator definitions mean the first pair of `a` and `b` is dead code and silently discarded.\n\nThe duplicate definitions of `a` and `b` mean Python silently discards the first version of each decorator at import time. While the file appears to be an isolated exercise script, the behavior is definitively wrong \u2014 any distinction between the first and second definitions would be lost without warning.\n\n09_test_github_wbe/git copy.py \u2014 the duplicate decorator definitions need to be resolved.\n</details>\n\n<details open><summary><h3>Important Files Changed</h3></summary>\n\n| Filename | Overview |\n|----------|----------|\n| 09_test_github_wbe/git copy.py | New file introducing a Pydantic Employee model and decorator examples; contains duplicate definitions of decorators `a` and `b` that silently shadow the originals, plus mismatched field description and deprecated Pydantic API usage. |\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details open><summary><h3>Flowchart</h3></summary>\n\n<a href=\"#gh-light-mode-only\">\n\n```mermaid\n%%{init: {'theme': 'neutral'}}%%\nflowchart TD\n    A[Module Load] --> B[Define Employee BaseModel]\n    B --> C[Instantiate employee_data]\n    C --> D[Define decorator a - 1st definition]\n    D --> E[Define decorator b - 1st definition]\n    E --> F[Define decorator a - 2nd definition\\nOVERWRITES 1st]\n    F --> G[Define decorator b - 2nd definition\\nOVERWRITES 1st]\n    G --> H[\"Apply @b \u2192 @a to c()\"]\n    H --> I[\"c() call\\nb.wrapper \u2192 a.wrapper \u2192 c body\"]\n```\n\n</a>\n<a href=\"#gh-dark-mode-only\">\n\n```mermaid\n%%{init: {'theme': 'base', 'themeVariables': {\"darkMode\": true, \"background\": \"#0d1117\", \"primaryColor\": \"#21262d\", \"primaryTextColor\": \"#e6edf3\", \"primaryBorderColor\": \"#8b949e\", \"lineColor\": \"#8b949e\", \"textColor\": \"#e6edf3\", \"edgeLabelBackground\": \"#161b22\", \"actorBkg\": \"#21262d\", \"actorBorder\": \"#8b949e\", \"actorTextColor\": \"#e6edf3\", \"actorLineColor\": \"#8b949e\", \"signalColor\": \"#8b949e\", \"signalTextColor\": \"#e6edf3\", \"noteBkgColor\": \"#373320\", \"noteBorderColor\": \"#d4a72c\", \"noteTextColor\": \"#f0e6c0\", \"labelBoxBkgColor\": \"#21262d\", \"labelBoxBorderColor\": \"#8b949e\", \"labelTextColor\": \"#e6edf3\", \"loopTextColor\": \"#e6edf3\", \"activationBkgColor\": \"#30363d\", \"activationBorderColor\": \"#8b949e\"}}}%%\nflowchart TD\n    A[Module Load] --> B[Define Employee BaseModel]\n    B --> C[Instantiate employee_data]\n    C --> D[Define decorator a - 1st definition]\n    D --> E[Define decorator b - 1st definition]\n    E --> F[Define decorator a - 2nd definition\\nOVERWRITES 1st]\n    F --> G[Define decorator b - 2nd definition\\nOVERWRITES 1st]\n    G --> H[\"Apply @b \u2192 @a to c()\"]\n    H --> I[\"c() call\\nb.wrapper \u2192 a.wrapper \u2192 c body\"]\n```\n\n</a>\n</details>\n\n<sub>Reviews (2): Last reviewed commit: [\"test acion flsg\"](https://github.com/rajnagani31/fastapi/commit/915561078d1bc4ef8bc044e413b680647d14e120) | [Re-trigger Greptile](https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=39203857)</sub>\n\n<!-- /greptile_comment -->",
